<title>ITALY: BNA '97 profit 20.8 bln lire vs 1.1 bln.</title>
<headline>BNA '97 profit 20.8 bln lire vs 1.1 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     20.8 vs     1.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		 21.5 vs     1.4</p>
<p>    Interest margin	     811.3 vs   806.2</p>
<p>    Money management income 1,155.5 vs 1,126.3</p>
<p>    Gross operating result    215.9 vs   157.1</p>
<p>    Savings share div    90 lire vs 0</p>
<p>    Preference share div 30 lire vs 0</p>
<p>    Personnel costs	     632.8 vs   657.1</p>
<p>    Client deposits	  17,735.0 vs (up 4.7 percent)</p>
<p>    Client loans	     15,895.0 vs (up 5.7 percent)</p>
<p>Note: - Banca Nazionale dell'Agricoltura is controlled by Banca di Roma.</p>
</text>
